e by arjuna. (Vana Parva, Chapter 271, Verse 27).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["supravRRiddha", "supravRddha", "supravRiddha", "supravRuddha", "supravṛddha", "సుప్రవృద్ధ", "ಸುಪ್ರವೃದ್ಧ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["supravRRiddha", "supravRddha", "supravRiddha", "supravRuddha", "supravṛddha", "సుప్రవృద్ధ", "ಸುಪ್ರವೃದ್ಧ"]}], "suprayoga": [{"id": "suprayogA", "headword": "सुप्रयोगा", "headword_slp1": "suprayogA", "fold": "suprayoga", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "सुप्रयोगा\n\nSUPRAYOGĀ . A river in india famous in the Purāṇas. This sacred river is considered to be the source of agni (fire). (Vana Parva, Chapter 222, Verse 25).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["suprayogaa", "suprayogā", "సుప్రయోగా", "ಸುಪ್ರಯೋಗಾ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["suprayogaa", "suprayogā", "సుప్రయోగా", "ಸುಪ್ರಯೋಗಾ"]}], "supriya": [{"id": "supriyA", "headword": "सुप्रिया", "headword_slp1": "supriyA", "fold": "supriya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "सुप्रिया\n\nSUPRIYĀ . An apsaras daughter of Kaśyapaprajāpati by Pradhā, daughter of dakṣa. (Ādi Parva Chapter 65, Verse 51). supriyā participated in the birthday celebrations of arjuna. (Ādi Parva, Chapter 122, Verse 63).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["supriyaa", "supriyā", "సుప్రియా", "ಸುಪ್ರಿಯಾ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["supriyaa", "supriyā", "సుప్రియా", "ಸುಪ್ರಿಯಾ"]}], "suptaGna": [{"id": "suptaGna", "headword": "सुप्तघ्न", "headword_slp1": "suptaGna", "fold": "suptaGna", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "सुप्तघ्न\n\nSUPTAGHNA . One of the seven sons of mālyavān the rākṣasa, by his wife sundarī. (See under sundarī, mālyavān and mālī).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["suptaghna", "సుప్తఘ్న", "ಸುಪ್ತಘ್ನ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["suptaghna", "సుప్తఘ్న", "ಸುಪ್ತಘ್ನ"]}], "supuYjika": [{"id": "supuYjika", "headword": "सुपुञ्जिक", "headword_slp1": "supuYjika", "fold": "supuYjika", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "सुपुञ्जिक\n\nSUPUÑJIKA . Son of vipracitti by siṁhikā. He was killed by paraśurāma. (brahmāṇḍa purāṇa, 3.6. 13-12).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["supu~njika", "supuñjika", "సుపుఞ్జిక", "ಸುಪುಞ್ಜಿಕ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["supu~njika", "supuñjika", "సుపుఞ్జిక", "ಸುಪುಞ್ಜಿಕ"]}], "supuRya": [{"id": "supuRyA", "headword": "सुपुण्या", "headword_slp1": "supuRyA", "fold": "supuRya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "सुपुण्या\n\nSUPUṆYĀ . A river in india famous in the Purāṇas. (bhīṣma parva, Chapter 221, Verse 9).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["supuNyaa", "supuṇyā", "సుపుణ్యా", "ಸುಪುಣ್ಯಾ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["supuNyaa", "supuṇyā", "సుపుణ్యా", "ಸುಪುಣ್ಯಾ"]}]}